By the results in Section~3 of \cite{Djo06}, there is a {\em self-coordinatized} set $C \subseteq M^{\mathrm{eq}}$, in the sense of Definition 3.3 in \cite{Djo06}, such that  egin{align} &	ext{ $M \subseteq C$, $C$ is $\emptyset$-definable;} \ &	ext{ there are $0 < r < \omega$ and $\emptyset$-definable sets $C_0 \subseteq C_1 \subseteq \ldots \subseteq C_r \subseteq C$ such that} 
onumber \ &	ext{ $C_0 = \emptyset$, and for every $n < r$ and every $a \in C_{n+1}$, $\mathrm{SU}(a/C_n) = 1$;} 
onumber \ &	ext{ for all $n \leq r$, if $a \in C_n$, $b \in M^{\mathrm{eq}}$ and $\mathrm{tp}(a) = \mathrm{tp}(b)$, then $b \in C_n$;} 
onumber \ &	ext{ only finitely many sorts are represented in $C$; and} 
onumber \ &	ext{ $M \subseteq C \subseteq \mathrm{acl}(C_r)$.} 
onumber \end{align}

